<newsitem itemid="47345" id="root" date="1996-09-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: London Forfaiting H1 pretax profit jumps.</title>
<headline>London Forfaiting H1 pretax profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.68		  vs 7.87</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.7		    vs 3.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     16.57		  vs 11.09</p>
<p>Sales of forfaiting</p>
<p> assets		     885.70		 vs 666.60</p>
<p> Trading income	   31.42		  vs 21.81</p>
<p> Net income		 27.85		  vs 19.40</p>
<p> Admin expenses	   11.28		  vs 8.31</p>
<p> Tax			  4.64		   vs 3.10</p>
<p> Net taxed		  11.92		  vs 7.99</p>
<p> Retained		   8.13		   vs 4.54</p>
<p>Retained profit</p>
<p> brought forward	  37.19		  vs 28.09</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 28</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Trade financing group London Forfaiting Company Plc said trading in the first two months of the second half has remained strong. It continues to invest in global expansion and expects the full benefit of this to show through in future years.</p>
<p>The company said it will negotiate further medium term financing facilities to fund a larger asset base and future business growth.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
